A||N||3||007DOUG||Extreme odor from battery, another weird one?||||5||
Z||000000||007DOUG||11-19-2000||09:19 PM||||Man, what is it with me and batteries this week. Last week I blew the side out of one (BTW, I replaced the alt and all is fine... again). Now this:<P>Totally different fiero, totally different battery. I stopped for gas, and heard a hiss. I assumed it was a pinhole in a coolant hose. I opened the trunk to find vapor (or smoke) coming from the vent in my battery. What a fricking stink. Like rotten eggs or something dead. The battery was very warm. <P>Weird part: the fiero still ran/started/drove/charged as she should. <P>Now what? I swear, if I have to replace one more battery this year I'll scream. This would be like #7<P><P>------------------<BR>5 Indy pace Cars<BR>84 T-top<BR>84 SE<BR>86 SE V6 153K<BR>2 86 GT's<BR>86 GT 3.4 Pearl White T-top<BR>2 88 GT's (twins)<P>However......<BR><I>"Time is my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||5
Z||000001||ponya||11-19-2000||09:39 PM||||Hey Doug, sounds to me that you will be buying a new battery soon. The rotten egg smell is from the acid escaping into the air. <BR>Happened to me recently, luckily I caught it before it exploded. The battery also was warm. After I got it out of the car, I took of the caps and could see that the plates were disintergrating. Knowing all the Fiero's you own, you might make a deal with the local battery guy. I hear that they are cheaper by the dozen.    Bob||||reg||13
Z||000002||Raydar||11-20-2000||11:22 AM||||Doug,<BR>There is a possibility that the alternator is overcharging the battery, if the regulator went south. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||11-20-2000||07:38 PM||||that battery is toast. check the charging system before putting in a new one.||||reg||1
